#shaders/lang/en_us.lang

#Profiles
profile.LOW = §aLow
profile.MEDIUM = §aMedium
profile.HIGH = §eHigh (Recommended)
profile.ULTRA = §4Ultra
profile.comment = One-click performance presets. Each tier only changes settings that cost GPU time (shadow resolution, cloud sampling, ambient occlusion, reflection quality and similar), and leaves every setting you tuned for personal taste untouched.

#Screens
screen.POSTPROC = Post Processing
screen.POSTPROC.comment = Everything layered on top of the finished world render: film-style color, camera-lens effects and edge smoothing.
screen.TONEMAP = Tone Mapping
screen.TONEMAP.comment = The overall "film look" of the game: how the scene's huge brightness range is squeezed down so your screen can display it.
screen.TONEMAP_AGX = AgX
screen.TONEMAP_AGX.comment = The AgX look plus its contrast, saturation and gamma. These apply only while AgX is the selected tone mapper.
screen.TONEMAP_OKLAB = OKLAB
screen.TONEMAP_OKLAB.comment = The OKLAB display transform's highlight roll-off. Applies only while OKLAB is the selected tone mapper.
screen.TONEMAP_REINHARD_GAMUT = Reinhard-Gamut
screen.TONEMAP_REINHARD_GAMUT.comment = Gamut, input scale, highlight reach and hue retention for Reinhard-Gamut. Applies only while that mode is selected.
screen.TONEMAP_REINHARD_AGX = Reinhard-AgX
screen.TONEMAP_REINHARD_AGX.comment = Gamut, input scale, shoulder and hue controls for Reinhard-AgX. Applies only while that mode is selected.
screen.TONEMAP_GT7 = GT7
screen.TONEMAP_GT7.comment = Path blend and the chroma-fade start and end of the GT7 tone mapper. Applies only while GT7 is selected.
screen.EXPOSURE = Exposure
screen.EXPOSURE.comment = Automatic eye adaptation (like a phone camera's auto brightness), a manual brightness offset, and the night-vision color effect.
screen.CAMERA = Camera & Effects
screen.CAMERA.comment = Camera-lens effects: focus blur, motion smear and glowing light sources.
screen.ANTIALIASING = Antialiasing
screen.ANTIALIASING.comment = Smooths jagged staircase edges and re-sharpens the image afterwards. TAA is temporal anti-aliasing, which blends many frames; CAS is AMD FidelityFX Contrast Adaptive Sharpening.
screen.LIGHTING = Lighting
screen.LIGHTING.comment = Reflections, bounced sunlight, shadows, corner darkening and light source strength.
screen.REFLECTION = Reflections
screen.REFLECTION.comment = Screen-space reflections on opaque surfaces: how far they reach, their quality, and where they fade into the sky sheen.
screen.GI = Global Illumination
screen.GI.comment = Bounced sunlight: light that lands on a surface and then softly tints everything around it. SSGI (screen-space global illumination) traces it on screen; RSM (reflective shadow map) computes it from the sun's shadow map.
screen.AMBIENT = Ambient Light
screen.AMBIENT.comment = A guaranteed minimum light level and the strength of artificial lights.
screen.SHADOWS = Shadows
screen.SHADOWS.comment = Shadow sharpness, realistic soft shadow edges, and sunlight shining through leaves.
screen.PCSS = PCSS Soft Shadows
screen.PCSS.comment = Contact-hardening soft shadows: the blocker search budget, the light-source angle PCSS assumes, and the sample count behind the penumbra. PCSS is percentage-closer soft shadows and PCF is percentage-closer filtering; both apply while PCSS is on.
screen.SHADOW_DEPTH = Shadow Depth
screen.SHADOW_DEPTH.comment = Depth tolerance, plus the two boosts that set how wide the soft-shadow blur may grow.
screen.PLANT_SSS = Plant Translucency
screen.PLANT_SSS.comment = Sunlight shining through leaves and thin plants, with its own step budget, thickness and direction controls. SSS stands for subsurface scattering.
screen.CONTACT = Contact Shadows
screen.CONTACT.comment = Short-range screen-space shadows that fill the seam where objects meet the ground or a wall. Overworld and End only.
screen.AO = Ambient Occlusion
screen.AO.comment = The soft darkening inside corners, crevices, and where objects meet the ground. GTAO is the horizon-based method, SSAO the hemisphere-sampling one.
screen.AO_GTAO = GTAO
screen.AO_GTAO.comment = Parameters of the horizon-based ambient occlusion. Used while the mode is GTAO.
screen.AO_SSAO = SSAO
screen.AO_SSAO.comment = Parameters of the hemisphere-sampling ambient occlusion, which is heavier but softer. Used while the mode is SSAO.
screen.AO_TEMPORAL_SETTINGS = AO History
screen.AO_TEMPORAL_SETTINGS.comment = How long the ambient occlusion history is trusted and how it reacts to movement, so the shading stays steady without smearing. Used while temporal accumulation is on.
screen.ENVIRONMENT = Environment
screen.ENVIRONMENT.comment = Clouds, water and haze.
screen.SKY = Sky
screen.SKY.comment = Stars and the atmosphere at the horizon.
screen.CLOUDS = Clouds
screen.CLOUDS.comment = True 3D volumetric clouds: their shape, motion and lighting.
screen.CLOUD_SHAPE = Cloud Shape
screen.CLOUD_SHAPE.comment = Where the cloud layer sits, how much of the sky it covers, how wide the weather pattern is, and how fast it drifts with the wind.
screen.CLOUD_DETAIL = Cloud Detail
screen.CLOUD_DETAIL.comment = The erosion that carves wispy edges and inner structure out of the base cloud shape.
screen.CLOUD_LIGHTING = Cloud Lighting
screen.CLOUD_LIGHTING.comment = How the cloud is lit: which light is traced, how far the light ray marches, and the forward and backward scattering that makes edges glow.
screen.CLOUD_MULTISCATTER = Cloud Multiple Scattering
screen.CLOUD_MULTISCATTER.comment = Light that bounces around inside the cloud, so thick bodies stay bright instead of turning grey. Also holds the sky-light term and the cirrus equivalent.
screen.CLOUD_QUALITY = Cloud Quality
screen.CLOUD_QUALITY.comment = Sampling budget, temporal upscaling and history age: the settings that trade cloud cost against stability.
screen.WATER = Water
screen.WATER.comment = Water reflections, wave detail and underwater light.
screen.WATER_SURFACE = Water Surface
screen.WATER_SURFACE.comment = Sample budgets for the two surface effects: the reflection ray march and the wave parallax search.
screen.EPIPOLAR = Volume Light Grid (Epipolar)
screen.EPIPOLAR.comment = Budget, reach and edge handling of the epipolar volume light grid that shadows the water column and the air.
screen.FOG = Fog
screen.FOG.comment = Distance haze and the mask that hides the edge of the loaded world. Air fog and boundary fog apply in the Overworld only.
screen.INFORMATION = Information
screen.INFORMATION.comment = Pack info: the open-source license, what the performance presets change, how to read setting help, and where the diagnostic views live.
screen.DEBUG = Debug Views
screen.DEBUG.comment = Diagnostic views for troubleshooting. Each one replaces part of the normal image; leave them at their defaults while playing.

