value.RSM_DEBUG.0 = Normal View
value.RSM_DEBUG.1 = Raw Irradiance
value.RSM_DEBUG.2 = Temporal Irradiance
value.RSM_DEBUG.3 = Filtered Irradiance
value.RSM_DEBUG.4 = History Frames
option.AMBIENT_FLOOR = Minimum Ambient Light
option.AMBIENT_FLOOR.comment = A small guaranteed light level added to every surface, so unlit caves and the deepest shadows keep a hint of visibility instead of pure black. 0 = fully realistic darkness.
option.SKY_AMBIENT_STRENGTH = Sky Ambient Strength
option.SKY_AMBIENT_STRENGTH.comment = Brightness of the sky's ambient (SH) light on every surface. It dims the flat sky fill on shaded sides while direct sunlight stays untouched, and the SH fallback that GI uses for directions the screen trace cannot cover scales with it. 1.0 = the raw sky SH irradiance.
option.TORCH_BRIGHTNESS = Block Light Brightness
option.TORCH_BRIGHTNESS.comment = Brightness of every block light source: torches, lanterns, glowstone, lava, redstone lamps and the rest. They all share one warm tint, so cool-colored sources are tinted warm as well. The tint itself does not change with this slider.
option.STAR_MAP = 4K Star Map
option.STAR_MAP.comment = Draws the night sky from a real NASA star map (4K texture) instead of the procedural star field. Off saves a little memory and draw cost, and is what the LOW and MEDIUM presets use.
option.STAR_MAP_INTENSITY = Star Brightness
option.STAR_MAP_INTENSITY.comment = Brightness of the night sky's stars. 0 = starless sky. When the 4K Star Map is off, this scales the procedural star field instead.
option.ATM_HORIZON_DIP = Horizon Dip
option.ATM_HORIZON_DIP.comment = Thickens the haze band at the horizon by extending the atmosphere below the ground line, so distant terrain melts into a denser, more realistic horizon haze.
value.ATM_HORIZON_DIP.0 = Off
value.ATM_HORIZON_DIP.1 = On
option.ATM_HORIZON_DIP_SCALE = Horizon Dip Depth (km)
option.ATM_HORIZON_DIP_SCALE.comment = How deep that horizon atmosphere reaches, in kilometres: higher = thicker horizon haze.
